{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvyVAtKX3KzSLq3XwSZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fitting the three bands to the full d⁵ quartet energy matrices gives Dq ≈ 750 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 824 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 3348 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Method.** Mn²⁺ is high-spin d⁵, so the ground state is ⁶A₁. The three bands are spin-forbidden transitions from ⁶A₁ to the quartet states ⁴T₁(G), ⁴T₂(G) and ⁴E(G).\n\nI built the full d⁵ Hamiltonian for the Ms = 3/2 manifold, which has 25 determinants. It contains the Coulomb repulsion, written with the Slater integrals F² = 49B + 7C and F⁴ = 63C/5, plus the octahedral crystal field. I then fitted Dq, B and C to the three observed energies by least squares. This treatment includes the mixing of the ⁴T₁, ⁴T₂ and ⁴E states from the G term with those from the P and D terms, which first-order formulas leave out.\n\n**Result.** The fit reproduces all three bands to within 10⁻¹⁰ cm⁻¹. This is expected, since three parameters are fitted to three energies, so the fit has no spare data to test it.\n\n- Dq ≈ 750 cm⁻¹ (10Dq ≈ 7500 cm⁻¹)\n- B ≈ 824 cm⁻¹\n- C ≈ 3348 cm⁻¹\n\nAs a check, the ⁴E energy is independent of Dq and equals 10B + 5C. That gives 8242 + 16738 = 24 980 cm⁻¹, which matches the observed band. The ratio C/B ≈ 4.06 is also typical for Mn²⁺.\n\n{\"Dq\": 750, \"B\": 824, \"C\": 3348, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Three quartet bands fitted exactly to the full d5 quartet energy matrices (with G/P/D mixing) give three parameters.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1626,"cache_read_input_tokens":6969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1626,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_i